      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX T2V quick 17f @ 24 fps (lab)\n\nWhat this graph does: Ultra-short T2V smoke: 17 frames @ 24 fps \u2248 0.7 s.\nModels: ltx distilled FP8 UNET + DualCLIP (gemma_3_12B_it_fp4_mixed + ltx-2.3_text_projection_bf16, type ltxv) + LTX23 video/audio VAEs (joint AV empty audio latents required before KSampler).\nSampler: euler \u00b7 simple \u00b7 CFG 1.0 \u00b7 16 steps \u00b7 17 frames @ 24.0 fps \u2248 0.7 s \u00b7 768\u00d7512.\nSaveImage prefix: ez_ltx_t2v_quick (frame sequence).\n\nPrompting (LTX-2.3 + Gemma DualCLIP):\n\u2022 Describe actions over time (camera path + subject/environment motion), not a static caption alone.\n\u2022 I2V: restate the still\u2019s content, then one clear camera move + micro-motion; keep identity stable.\n\u2022 T2V: chronological shot description; one primary camera move for short clips.\n\u2022 Negatives target temporal artifacts (morphing, flicker, jitter) when you experiment with CFG > 1.\n\nHow to run:\n1. Review Positive prompt; queue.\n2. Encode frames \u2192 MP4 with ffmpeg (below).\n\nOUTPUT = FRAMES, NOT MP4\nThis lab saves a PNG sequence via SaveImage (prefix above). VideoHelperSuite (VHS) is NOT installed.\n\nTo get a playable video on the host (24 fps lab default):\n  ffmpeg -y -framerate 24 -pattern_type glob -i 'ez_ltx_t2v_quick_*.png' \\\n    -c:v libx264 -pix_fmt yuv420p -crf 18 out.mp4\nFind frames under Comfy\u2019s output folder (container volume / mapped host path).\nOptional in-Comfy MP4: install ComfyUI-VideoHelperSuite and add VHS_VideoCombine after VAEDecode.\nAudio: LTX-2.3 uses empty joint-AV audio latents; lab does not decode/save audio.\n\nJoint AV note: LTXVEmptyLatentAudio + LTXVConcatAVLatent are required for KSampler; LTXVSeparateAVLatent then video VAEDecode + SaveImage (audio latent unused)."
      ],
      "title": "LTX T2V quick 17f @ 24 fps (lab) \u2014 operator note"
    }
